course: dictionary
lesson: 10015
title: Tempt: pulling you towards something
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To tempt someone is to make them want to do or have something, often something they should not. The thing that tempts you looks nice, so it pulls you towards it. «Theo was tempted to make a second account himself.» Theo wanted to do something he knew he should not, and the idea pulled at him.
explain: Tempt has other forms: tempts, tempted and tempting. Tempting means so nice that it is hard to say no, as in «tempting offer». When you meet tempt, look at the words around it. If someone is offering you something nice and you feel a pull to say yes, the word is tempt.
explain: Tempt can also mean trying to get someone to do something by offering them something nice. In a fairy tale, the witch tempts Hansel and Gretel with sweets. The words with, offer and nice are the clues that tempt is about luring someone with a treat.
fact: Tempt means to make someone want to do or have something, especially something they should not.
fact: «Tempting» food or offers are hard to resist.
fact: «Be tempted to» means feel a pull to do something. «Tempt someone with» means offer them something nice to get them to do it.
fact: «Don't tempt fate» means don't take a risk that might go wrong.
fact: Tricky people may tempt children with sweets, games or gifts. If you are tempted, say no and tell a trusted adult.
exercise: «Theo was tempted to make a second account himself.» What does tempted mean here? | He was sound asleep | He was sure to be bored all afternoon | He was made to stay behind by the teacher | *He felt a strong pull to do something he should not
exercise: In the fairy tale the witch tempts Hansel and Gretel with sweets. What is the witch trying to do? | Teach them how to bake | Help them find their way home | Make them go to sleep at once | *Lure them in with something nice
exercise: Find and copy the word that means very nice and hard to resist: «The shop had tempting cakes in the window.» | cakes | *tempting | shop | window
test: What does «tempt someone with» mean? | To make them laugh until they cry | To hide something from them | *To offer them something nice to get them to do something | To run away from them
test: A stranger offers you sweets and a game if you go with them. What should you do? | Go with them, because the sweets look nice | Take the sweets and decide later | Keep it secret and go along later | *Say no and tell a trusted adult
exam: «Don't tempt fate» most likely means: | Don't be late for the bus | Don't tell anyone your name | *Don't take a risk that might go wrong | Don't eat anything sweet
